Track 2: Sinking the Pit-Prop
- Story & Context: Senior foreman Hauer sat on an inverted wooden crate, confessing to his crew that he had intentionally missed his own daughter's wedding rehearsal to cover an extra shift down below. His voice drifted through a low-pass filter of dripping water and slow-swinging cassette vinyl crackle while a trumpet wailed softly in a Dorian scale. The rhythmic hiss of a leaky hydraulic line provided the track’s lazy, swinging hi-hat, giving his confession a strange, tragic warmth. "I traded her calendar days for a bucket of coal," he whispered into his brass headlamp, holding a faded photograph up to the yellow light.
